      "summary": "ATLAS-COUPLING: the V-quantifier of the seam, MEASURED. ADVANCED, NO GATE CLOSED (ajcr-p1, run 0087 r2).\n\nTHE ROW TITLE WAS WRONG IN THE LETTER, RIGHT IN THE SUBSTANCE. It said coverage must land in the SAME V as hf. Correct statement: NESTED opens Vc <= Vf suffice (pic0RepresentableBy_of_nested) -- and that generalisation is EQUIVALENT to the shared-V form (nested_iff_shared), so the nesting is not freedom.\n\nLANDED, Picard/Pic0ChartVMonotone.lean, rooted at AlgebraicJacobian.lean:575, sorry-free, lake build EXIT=0 (8894 jobs), ALL 13 declarations axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] vs a control firing sorryAx:\n * isChartUniv_antitone -- antecedent 1 is ANTITONE in V. So isChartUniv_bot is free because bot is the EASIEST value, not because of the empty scheme: the Sat.lean endpoint becomes structural.\n * isLocallySurjective_sigmaDesc_mono -- antecedent 2 is MONOTONE, at the level of the INSTANCE the seam consumes, not the hcov spelling. The coproduct step is sigmaDesc_restrictChart_le + mathlib isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective.\n * isLocallySurjective_unrestricted -- antecedent 2 at ANY V implies UNRESTRICTED coverage. So the restriction relieves antecedent 1 (bot is free) and antecedent 2 by NOTHING: a coverage lane cannot buy relief by restricting, whichever open it names. CHEAP, one rfl plus one mathlib lemma -- I first called this the file substantive content and that was wrong (I-1117).\n * isLocallySurjective_of_bot -- CLOSES the loophole Sat.lean:93-98 left open, from the other side: inhabiting the instance binder at bot yields unrestricted coverage. Not a cheap route.\n * coverage_instance_of_nested -- the UPWARD collapse. Needs no antitonicity, so it composes with RestrictedChartFibre at Vf DIRECTLY and recovers the NAMED representing object rather than a Sigma.\n\nTWO REASONS OF MINE, RETRACTED at their sites after a fresh-context audit:\n (1) I-1117: iso-ness of Scheme.topIso is NEVER USED anywhere in the file; and only one implication is proved, not an equivalence.\n (2) I-1119: opposite monotonicities do NOT squeeze the pair. EITHER monotonicity alone gives the collapse. True form: a nesting generalisation buys nothing as soon as ONE hypothesis is monotone in the direction the nesting relaxes.\n\nLEVEL CAVEAT, and it decides what nested_iff_shared retires: it is stated at IsOpenImmersion.presheaf for an ARBITRARY chart family, while the assembly consumes RestrictedChartFibre at the ABEL family. Monotonicity of RestrictedChartFibre ITSELF is proved NOWHERE in the tree -- only its IsChartUniv consequence. The assembly-level collapse runs through coverage_instance_of_nested instead.\n\nNOT CLOSED. rep has no producer, so IsChartUniv is not statable without it; no chart is built at any V but bot; and INHABITATION OF THE PAIR (huniv V, hcov V) IS UNMEASURED AT EVERY V. This round removed a candidate escape from that question, it did not answer it. That question still gates the whole antecedent-1 side.",
